HTTP responses: Status Line and Status Codes
Every first line of http responses called Status line.
Status line consisted with HTTP version, Status code, Reason Phrase.
In status line, Status code means short three-digit numbers that showing the outcome of request
Reason Phrase is short message that explains the status code.

Common status codes : 
100 : continue(waiting additional response)
200 : OK
301 : Moved permanantly
404 : Not found
500 : Internal Server Error

Response Header
Key headers in response header : Content-type / Content=length / Date
Content-type : what kind of content it's getting. like HTML,JSON. also includes character set (like UTF-8)

Other Common Response Headers
Set-cookie : sends cookies from the server to the client.
To keep things secure, cookie must set with the HttpOnly / Secure flag.
Cache-control: tells how long it can cache the response before checking with the server again

Security Headers
helps improve the overall security of the web application by providing mitigations(완화)
Content-Security-Policy (CSP)
An additional security layer that can help mitigate against common attacks like Cross-Site Scripting(XSS).
CSP provides a way for administrators to say what domains or sources are considered safe and provides a layer of mitigation to such attacks.

Strict-Transport-Security(HSTS)
Ensures that web browsers will always connect over HTTPS.
ex)[Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload]
max-age : expiry time

X-Content-Type-Options
Instruct browsers not to guess MIME time of a resource but only use the Content-type header.
nonsniff : not to sniff or guess MIME type.
*MIME type: Internet standard that extends the format of email messages to support text in character sets other than ASCII


